# Pre-upgrade audit: launchpad authorization, delivery and qualification tools.

[audit.22.30.29]
task = "22.30.29"
revision = "0f3fe6b8c5c1973c0e80408097cf66e06e40785f"
files_reviewed = 111
findings = 49
docs_reviewed = 16
upgrade_ready = false
blocking = ["active-rebuild-restart"]
review_basis = "Contract reconciliation at the recorded revision against all 111 package members, preserving the original whole-file audit and its unresolved findings. Registry contracts/ links resolve relative to spec/layerx-merge, not the repository root. Static comparisons do not qualify application behavior, dependency closure, provider workloads or capacity; only the task documentation gate is declared for this reconciliation."
prior_revision = "6d2c32a65a1c7989a6a37abf5965929de9769ae4"
retained_findings_basis = "The original 41 findings retain their original observation revision, severity and ownership pending owning-domain qualification evidence. Current source changes are identified in current_review and file notes; retaining a finding does not assert that its historical observed code is still present. In particular active-rebuild-restart remains the sole high finding and blocker; this documentation-only gate cannot close it."
clients_comparison = "All 54 client members: file.001 is the slippage widget; file.002 through file.028 are the 27 auth members; file.029 through file.054 are the 26 delivery members. Compared with spec/layerx-merge/contracts/clients.md:319 (shared Go interface group) and :739 (web group). SlippageSelector delegates settings and computeMinOut to the shared trade domain at apps/launchpad/web/src/widgets/trade/slippage-selector.tsx:12 and :16; this widget declares no receipt authority. Auth carries EIP-191/ERC1271 wallet proofs, signed HTTP operations, identity assertions, session checks, mTLS and immutable audit effects, not a mandatory DID-bound transaction per operation. Delivery carries schema-1 chain-125 envelopes, transactional outbox/inbox effects, durable broker acknowledgements, ordered partitions, archive/replay generations, scoped shadow comparisons and HTTPS webhook cursors. The implementations and their Go/SQL/test members were compared as producer, persistence and consumer groups; clients.md:13 and :19 omit or misdescribe these boundaries (clients-offchain-operations, clients-receipt-authority)."
services_comparison = "Compared all 27 auth and 26 delivery members plus the service-facing load signer/HTTP/feeder/browser/receiver and phase runners against spec/layerx-merge/contracts/services.md:25, :260 and :337. Named unavailable refusals, signed eth_sendRawTransaction writes, mTLS requests, raw-body HMAC webhooks and persisted retry/cursor identities agree with the applicable refusal/write/security intent. services.md:28 still requires separate sequencer ReceiptKeys for every receipt, unlike the node-reported block identities used by auth and load. services.md:346 and :347 omit the archive and generation recovery prerequisites implemented by NewArchive and ReplayEngine. The scoped disagreements are services-receipt-authority and services-recovery-contract, not proposals to restore a sequencer/router or to bypass provenance checks."
tooling_comparison = "All 57 tool members: file.055 through file.078 are the 24 interface-tool members, and file.079 through file.111 are the 33 load-tool members. The tooling heading is spec/layerx-merge/contracts/launchpad.md:6820; the relevant tools group is :7040, with production rows beginning at :7090 and this slice at :7302 through :7425. Compared required options, environment inputs, executable entry points, imported helpers, Solidity/ERC1271 fixtures, deployment identity generation, evidence schemas/manifests, fixed-arrival workloads and configured provider tests. Accounting options :7303 agree with accounting_check.py:215; phase runner configuration/output options :7396 and :7401 agree with their current parsers; the JSON policies still explicitly refuse capacity qualification. Source-authority option drift and import-only modules presented as commands are concrete findings launchpad-tool-authority-options and launchpad-library-commands. Phase-2 and phase-3 manifest qualifier paths add load-phase2-qualification-command and load-phase3-qualification-command; phase-4 now names the merged specification at phase-4-scenario-manifest.json:116."
acceptance_comparison = "Package criteria 4498.1, 4499.1 and 4499.2 agree statically with client-deployment.test.cjs:6, :8, :18 and :47 and client-deployment.cjs:17 through :29: the suite supplies the repository contracts root without CONTRACT_SOURCE_ROOT, the helper carries kind/runtime and implementation identities, and role-address drift is refused. This agrees with the capabilities at spec/layerx-merge/contracts/launchpad.md:7454 and :7455; no deployment test was executed. The operations criteria at launchpad.md:6848 through :6852, shared-config criteria at clients.md:346 and :347, web criteria at clients.md:811 through :836, and service criteria at services.md:323 through :335 and :383 through :384 name tests outside this member slice; they are not satisfied by these file verdicts. Criterion 22998.1 requires executed sweep commands and 22076.1 requires manifest/lockfile advisory and frozen-install evidence outside this slice; neither is claimed by static comparison."

