[doc.14]
path = "spec/layerx-merge/contracts/launchpad.md"
status = "misleading"
notes = "spec/layerx-merge/contracts/launchpad.md:6820 is existing tooling prose, :7040 is the tools interface group, and :7090 begins production-tool rows; :7302 through :7425 cover this slice. Compared all 24 interface-tool and 33 load-tool members, including schemas/manifests/tests and required parser inputs. Accounting inputs and phase runner --config/--config-sha256/--output names agree; source-authority defaults/environment rows :7311 through :7364 are stale and import-only modules at :7368, :7369, :7379, :7388 through :7394, :7399, :7410, :7411 and :7425 are misleading cli_command entries (launchpad-tool-authority-options, launchpad-library-commands). The :7454/:7455 client deployment capabilities agree statically with 4498.1/4499.1/4499.2 and current client-deployment source/tests. Operations criteria at :6848 through :6852 are outside the slice, not missing pages or evidence of qualification. Phase-2/3 qualifier path disagreements are recorded against their manifests; no deployment, workload or capacity gate ran."

[doc.15]
path = "spec/layerx-merge/contracts/clients.md"
status = "misleading"
notes = "spec/layerx-merge/contracts/clients.md:319 covers the 27 auth and 26 delivery members and :739 covers the one web widget; the shared/interface and web acceptance tables at :342 and :807 name tests outside this slice. Auth uses EIP-191/ERC1271 wallet proofs and signed HTTP mutation/session assertions (operation.go:62, ledger.go:60, contract.go:116); delivery uses durable envelopes, broker acknowledgements, PostgreSQL generations and scoped shadow proofs. The exhaustive operation list :13/:17 omits those off-chain effects (clients-offchain-operations), while :19 through :30 and :49 through :51 prescribe retired sequencer rungs/ReceiptKeys and :20 a router, unlike reported_hash_backend.go:65 and phase2_feeder.py:99 through :118 (clients-receipt-authority). SlippageSelector and computeMinOut delegate to shared trade settings/domain and introduce no receipt authority. No unrelated receipt or web acceptance test is claimed to cover these members."

[doc.16]
path = "spec/layerx-merge/contracts/services.md"
status = "misleading"
notes = "spec/layerx-merge/contracts/services.md:27 and :29 agree with named refusals and signed chain writes, and :30 is consistent with reference-based webhook secrets. Compared auth, delivery and load service consumers with :260 through :335 (gateway group and criteria) and :337 through :384 (indexer group and criteria). The universal ReceiptKeys rule :28 and sequencer/router catalogue :39 contradict node-root committed-block authority used by auth/contract.go:67 and load/phase2_feeder.py:114 (services-receipt-authority). The height-only recovery description :347/:352 omits archive provenance, generation/lease/alias and shadow-proof requirements in delivery/archive.go:55, replay.go:53/:106 and shadow.go:103 (services-recovery-contract). Gateway criteria :323/:324 exercise auth measurements outside this slice and indexer criteria :383/:384 cover ABI parity, not replay restart qualification. Existing high active-rebuild-restart remains blocking pending owning-domain evidence; no new service or missing-page repair is proposed."
